course: dictionary
lesson: 15884
title: Unintelligible: when words cannot be understood
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Unintelligible means you cannot understand it. The words may be there, but they are unclear, mumbled, too messy to read, or in a language you do not know. «The announcement on the station was unintelligible because of the echo.» You know someone was speaking, but you could not make out what they said.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. Ask yourself: could I understand this? If the answer is no, and the reason is mumbling, a bad signal, messy writing or a language you do not know, then unintelligible is the right word. «His handwriting was so messy that the note was unintelligible.»
explain: Unintelligible is about understanding, not about being right or wrong. Words can be unintelligible even if they would be true. «The phone line cut out, and her reply was unintelligible.» To check, put "could not be understood" in place of the hard word. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the meaning.
fact: Unintelligible means impossible to understand.
fact: Unintelligible is an adjective, so you can write «unintelligible speech» or «unintelligible writing».
fact: The start un- means not, and intelligible means clear enough to understand, so unintelligible means not clear enough to understand.
fact: Things that can be unintelligible include mumbling, bad phone lines, messy handwriting, noisy announcements and foreign languages.
fact: Unintelligible tells you the words could not be understood, not that they were wrong.
exercise: «The old man mumbled, and his words were unintelligible.» What does unintelligible mean here? | Written in neat handwriting | Very loud and clear | Full of jokes | *Could not be understood
exercise: «The bad phone line made her voice unintelligible.» Why could Sam not understand her? | She was telling a joke | She spoke in a language Sam had learned at school | *The line was bad and her words were lost | She was writing a note
exercise: Ravi says unintelligible means wrong. Why is he mistaken? | It means the words are wrong and must be fixed | *It means the words cannot be understood, not that they are wrong | It means the same as silent | It means very funny
test: «The words of the song were unintelligible to the class.» Why were the words unintelligible? | The words were all rhymes | The song had no words | The singer was too quiet to hear | *The class did not know the language the song was sung in
test: Which sentence uses unintelligible correctly? | The teacher's joke was unintelligible, so we all laughed at once | *The radio static was so loud that the weather report was unintelligible | Her coat was unintelligible | The sun was unintelligible
exam: «The baby babbled happily, and her words were unintelligible.» What does unintelligible mean? | *Could not be understood | Happy and bright | Clear and well-spoken | Very quiet and sleepy
